  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sucralfate is an anti-ulcer medicine used to treat stomach and duodenal ulcers, gastritis, gastroesophageal reflux disease, esophagitis, and related mouth and gut conditions. It is an approved drug, widely used for acid-related digestive disorders, though it is not authorised centrally in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420394&quot;>Wikidata Q420394</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sucralfate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A02BX02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00364&quot;>DB00364</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/70789197&quot;>70789197</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420394&quot;>Q420394</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C11H44Al8O51S8</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>1464.76 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
